Wrote the single-topic row (housing) to coder-3.json. Michael Carbone was prime sponsor of HB2720 (2024), which he also voted Yea on final passage — a law barring municipalities from imposing ADU zoning restrictions stricter than for single-family homes. That's a chair-shaped match to rung 5 ("cut the regulations and zoning limits that block private building"), so I coded v6_value: 5, resting on all three snapshots (bill text, sponsor listing, vote page).
